     "\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div lang=\"EN-AU\" link=\"#0563C1\" vlink=\"#954F72\" style=\"word-wrap:break-word\">\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Hi folks,<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">I use openCR 1.4 (I dealt with earlier issues raised here by reverting back to openCR 1.4) to estimate D and phi for a social, warren living species in an 1100ha enclosure.<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">I no longer get any errors when I use JSSAsecrD models, and if I do I can deal with them by raising the iteration limit.<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">My question is: should I model both sexes simultaneously or create separate capthist objects for males and females? I know the sexes have different movement patterns across the landscape and we have strong indication that survival rates\r\n differ between the sexes. My estimates of D when my capthist includes all individuals with no grouping covariates looks very similar to the output from a capthist that only includes females (see table).<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Should I derive total D from the model with no grouping covariate or should I sum the results of my male and female models? Secr.fit generates results that are somewhere in between.<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<table border=\"1\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse;border:none\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td width=\"156\" valign=\"top\" style=\"width:116.85pt;border:solid windowtext 1.0pt;padding:0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Package<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td width=\"156\" valign=\"top\" style=\"width:116.85pt;border:solid windowtext 1.0pt;border-left:none;padding:0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">D, no grouping covariate<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td width=\"156\" valign=\"top\" style=\"width:116.85pt;border:solid windowtext 1.0pt;border-left:none;padding:0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Male only capthist<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td width=\"156\" valign=\"top\" style=\"width:116.9pt;border:solid windowtext 1.0pt;border-left:none;padding:0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Female only capthist<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td width=\"156\" valign=\"top\" style=\"width:116.9pt;border:solid windowtext 1.0pt;border-left:none;padding:0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Sum male and female outputs<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td width=\"156\" rowspan=\"5\" valign=\"top\" style=\"width:116.85pt;border:solid windowtext 1.0pt;border-top:none;padding:0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">openCR 1.4<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">JSSAsecrD<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td width=\"156\" valign=\"top\" style=\"width:116.85pt;border-top:none;border-left:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;border-right:solid windowtext 1.0pt;padding:0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">0.58<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td width=\"156\" valign=\"top\" style=\"width:116.85pt;border-top:none;border-left:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;border-right:solid windowtext 1.0pt;padding:0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">0.48<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td width=\"156\" valign=\"top\" style=\"width:116.9pt;border-top:none;border-left:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;border-right:solid windowtext 1.0pt;padding:0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">0.60<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td width=\"156\" valign=\"top\" style=\"width:116.9pt;border-top:none;border-left:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;border-right:solid windowtext 1.0pt;padding:0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">1.08<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td width=\"156\"